# pronative.ai OpenCode Observability Plugin

OpenCode plugin that captures and sends OpenCode session telemetry to Langfuse. It traces user turns, assistant generations, tool calls, retries, reasoning output, compaction output, and failed generation steps.

## Quick Start

Enable the plugin and add your telemetry credentials in `.opencode/opencode.jsonc` (or `opencode.json`):

```jsonc
{
  "experimental": {
    "openTelemetry": true,
  },
  "plugin": ["@pronative.ai/opencode-observability-plugin@latest"],
  "otel": {
    "publicKey": "pk-lf-...",
    "secretKey": "sk-lf-...",
    "baseUrl": "https://cloud.langfuse.com",
    "environment": "development",
    "userId": "your-user-id",
    "attributes": "style=adhoc;attempt=1,name=test;",
  },
}
```

Restart OpenCode after changing the configuration.

## Configuration Reference

The `otel` section in your `.opencode/opencode.jsonc` or `opencode.json` accepts the following properties:

| Property      | Type                 | Required | Default                      | Description                                                                                                                     |
| ------------- | -------------------- | -------- | ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `publicKey`   | `string`             | **Yes**  | —                            | Your Langfuse public API key (`pk-lf-...`)                                                                                      |
| `secretKey`   | `string`             | **Yes**  | —                            | Your Langfuse secret API key (`sk-lf-...`)                                                                                      |
| `baseUrl`     | `string`             | No       | `https://cloud.langfuse.com` | Langfuse host URL (use your self-hosted URL if applicable)                                                                      |
| `environment` | `string`             | No       | `training`                   | Deployment environment tag (e.g. `production`, `staging`)                                                                       |
| `userId`      | `string`             | No       | —                            | Identifier for attributing traces to a specific user                                                                            |
| `serviceName` | `string`             | No       | `opencode`                   | OpenTelemetry service name                                                                                                      |
| `attributes`  | `string` \| `object` | No       | —                            | Custom OpenTelemetry span/resource attributes. Supports delimited string (`,` or `;`, e.g. `"k1=v1;k2=v2"`) or key-value object |

> [!TIP]
> Both `.jsonc` and `.json` file formats are supported in `.opencode/` or in the root project folder. Single-line (`//`) and multi-line (`/* */`) comments as well as trailing commas are supported in `.jsonc`.

## Sample Configuration (with AgentGateway)

Below is a complete `.opencode/opencode.jsonc` configured with the observability plugin, Langfuse credentials, and the Pronative AgentGateway provider:

```json
{
  "experimental": {
    "openTelemetry": true
  },
  "plugin": ["@pronative.ai/opencode-observability-plugin@latest"],
  "otel": {
    "publicKey": "pk-lf-...",
    "secretKey": "sk-lf-...",
    "baseUrl": "https://cloud.langfuse.com",
    "environment": "development",
    "userId": "your-user-id",
    "attributes": {
      "k1": "v1",
      "k2": "v2"
    }
  },
  "provider": {
    "agentgateway": {
      "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
      "name": "AgentGateway",
      "options": {
        "baseURL": "https://<your-agent-gateway-url>",
        "apiKey": "<your-agentgateway-api-key>"
      },
      "models": {
        "DeepSeek-V4-Pro": {
          "name": "DeepSeek V4 Pro"
        },
        "gpt-5.4": {
          "name": "gpt-5.4"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Supported Versions

Validated OpenCode versions:

- `1.15.13`
- `1.18.19`

